{"name":"Puddle","hex":"#a0a6a0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"puddle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, often temporary, pool of water, usually on a path or road. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Stagnant or polluted water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form a puddle.","To play or splash in a puddle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puddle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Puddle","blocks":[{"text":"A puddle is a small accumulation of liquid, usually water, on a surface. It can form either by pooling in a depression on the surface, or by surface tension upon a flat surface. Puddles are often characterized by murky water or mud due to the disturbance and dissolving of surrounding sediment, primarily due to precipitation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Begliktash_puddle_%D0%91%D0%B5%D0%B3%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%BA%D1%82%D0%B0%D1%88_%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BA%D0%B2%D0%B0_%E2%80%94_%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BF%D0%B8%D1%8F.jpg/330px-Begliktash_puddle_%D0%91%D0%B5%D0%B3%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%BA%D1%82%D0%B0%D1%88_%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BA%D0%B2%D0%B0_%E2%80%94_%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BF%D0%B8%D1%8F.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puddle","wikidata":"Q152841"},{"title":"Puddle (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Puddle is a puzzle-platform game developed by Neko Entertainment and published by Konami for PlayStation Vita, PlayStation 3, PlayStation 4 and Xbox 360. The game was also self-published by Neko Entertainment for Wii U, and for the PC through Steam, GOG.com, and Desura."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6e/Puddle_%28video_game%29_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puddle_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q3925373"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Tadorna_tadorna_%28Tadorne_de_B